# Ceph.Sec replay.
#
# `cephsec --replay <this file>` plays it back and checks every mark. A mark
# is the event digest and the world digest at the end of that tick; if either
# differs, playback stops and says which, and when.
#
# Ticks are 60 to the second and restart at zero for each segment, because a
# level transition resets the world clock. '#' starts a comment only as the
# first character of a line.
cephsec-replay 1
game m4-replay
catalogue 879300ddc9d0ca82

segment recon-sweep cef5ec
at 30 cmd nmap -sn 10.0.4.0/24
at 300 mark 396cca8c332a91a6 15833f3318a9bc69
at 600 mark 396cca8c332a91a6 8f5755785005c8bc
at 900 mark 396cca8c332a91a6 37542a9ea377437b
at 900 cmd objectives
at 960 cmd play 2
at 960 mark b7e2fe5f62ce2716 1b135148247c74f7

